You own the copyright to that work, because the university did not 
provide the funds you refer to as financial aid (which can mean any 
number of things, but IMO is most properly used to describe need-based 
aid) to you in the expectation that you would provide them a novel in 
return. If, however, you recieved a grant from the english department 
specifically to write a novel, then the school probably owns the 
copyright. It should also be pointed out that _most_ financial aid does 
_not_ have to be used to purchase services from the university (ie, you 
could use it to pay for rent, food, or whatever else you chose), and so 
you are merely using funds that you have the full legal rights to to rent 
computer time from the university. (In the case of USC, this is actually 
a specific billed item seperate from tuition, making this relationship 
rather clearer than it may be where this is not the case.)


