Internet Good or Bad?

The internet is a wealth of information, it is also a host for
immortality.  The internet is a way of accessing information from all
over the world.  This information can be good and bad.  A friend of mine
who has access through the University [of Alberta] lead me through the
world of the Internet.  What I [Doug Sydora] found out was startling. 

Among other things, we found a list of topics that were a little bit
disturbing.  A few of these were necrophelia, and child pornography
[Doug doesn't want to admit the other related newsgroups that he checked
out].  An Internet suscriber can call up these files which often contain
pictures.  And yes to our total suprise it is possible to bring up
pictures of 12 and 13 year old girls nude.  

This took me [Doug Sydora] by total suprise, I [Doug Sydora] always 
envisioned the internet as a way to look up topics from other sources
like libraries and information banks, not a way for pedophiles to get
off.  The picture of the young girl that we brought up [Why is Doug
Sydora and his University friend looking at these pictures if they are
offended by them] had a caption on it.  It said something to the effect
of "Hundreds more teenage pics available."

So what do you think [a NAIT student who has no access to the internet]?
The Internet can be a way to communicate with people who share your
interests, it can be a way to access information from all over the
world, italso can be a way to see illegal pornography.  Good or Bad?
You [a NAIT student who has no access to the internet] decide.

